(function(payload){if(typeof applySerialChapterPayload==="function")applySerialChapterPayload(payload);else (window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE||(window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE=[])).push(payload);})({"id":"serial-mystery-01","version":"0a6b940755c1","book":"seventh-wharf","cn":["客车碾过泥泞的江堤，程雾撑着黑伞在出站口接我。我从内袋掏出今早收到的[[anonymous|匿名的]]信，牛皮纸[[envelope|信封]]已经被雨浸软。里面是一张旧船票、一把铜钥匙和一张新字条：‘潮退以后，听第七声。先找赵启。’我突然的[[arrival|到来]]恰逢河灯节，沿岸亮着一串纸灯，旧[[harbour|港口]]却隐在雨幕后，像一只合拢的手。程雾问我吃饭没有。我摇头，只怕再晚一步，那张票上的地方也会消失。","我们顶着风拐进修船铺。程雾是来采录河灯节声音的，也是我从小吵到大的[[companion|同伴]]。老陈正替人[[repair|修理]]发动机，看见船票，扳手停在半空。他从柜中取出一盘装在塑料盒里的[[cassette|磁带]]，说那是父亲留在船上的东西，旧播放机坏后，他一直不敢拿去乱试。墙上合影补齐了当年的[[background|背景]]：父亲掌舵，老陈修船，赵启管理港务档案；那时负责调度的秦衡，如今成了港史馆负责人。","炭火一响，老陈把茶壶从炉上移开。关于事故的[[rumour|传言]]二十年没断，有人说父亲喝醉了，有人说水底的[[ghost|鬼魂]]会拉船。窗外的改造告示写着，B[[warehouse|仓库]]即将清运，旁边还拿‘夜半湿脚印’招揽游客。秦衡曾向老陈保证，小镇从来只有六个泊位。可票上明明印着第七[[wharf|码头]]。老陈指着河湾，低声说那是旧浮台的叫法，并非一座正式登记的码头；没有画在新地图上，不等于它从未存在。","台灯下，船票背面浮出另一行铅笔字：‘忙完这一回，带阿舟看海。’我认出父亲末笔向上挑的[[handwriting|笔迹]]，手指却不敢碰纸。程雾先拍下正反面，提醒我，要[[identify|辨认]]寄信人，不能凭一行熟悉的字。船票可能是[[authentic|真实的]]旧物，新字条却来自今天的人，两者得分开看。赵启的电话一直无人接，老陈上午约他喝茶也没等到。这才是第一条能核对的[[clue|线索]]。","铺里的电话响了。赵启妻子说，他前晚去港务楼后就像[[disappear|消失]]了一样，只留下要到旧[[archive|档案库]]核对材料的话。她已经报了警，何警官请我们保存寄件信息，别自行追人。找人的事突然变得[[urgent|紧急]]。我刚记下他的电话，河对岸便传来六下钟响；隔了半分钟，第七下低低落进雨里，像一个从B库发出的[[signal|信号]]。老陈捏住我的袖子：‘不是祠堂的钟。先站在亮处听。’"],"en":["The bus jolted along the muddy embankment. Cheng Wu met me outside the station with a black umbrella. I took out the [[anonymous|anonymous]] letter I had received that morning; rain had softened its brown-paper [[envelope|envelope]]. Inside were an old ferry ticket, a copper key, and a new note: 'After the tide falls, listen for the seventh sound. Find Zhao Qi first.' My unexpected [[arrival|arrival]] coincided with the lantern festival. Paper lights lined the bank, but the old [[harbour|harbour]] hid behind the rain like a closed hand. Cheng asked whether I had eaten. I shook my head, afraid the place on the ticket would vanish before I reached it.","We hurried through the wind into Chen's repair shop. Cheng had come to record the festival; she was also the childhood [[companion|companion]] I had always argued with. Chen was working to [[repair|repair]] an engine. His wrench stopped when he saw the ticket. He brought a [[cassette|cassette]] in a plastic case out of a cupboard. It had belonged to Dad, he said. Since his old player broke, he had been afraid to try it in another machine. A photograph on the wall supplied the [[background|background]]: Dad steered the ferry, Chen repaired boats, and Zhao managed port records. Qin Heng, then responsible for dispatch, now ran the port-history museum.","The charcoal crackled. Chen moved the teapot off the stove. Every [[rumour|rumour]] about the accident had survived twenty years: Dad had been drunk, or a [[ghost|ghost]] beneath the river had pulled his boat under. A redevelopment notice outside said that [[warehouse|warehouse]] B would soon be cleared. Beside it, an advertisement used 'midnight wet footprints' to attract visitors. Qin had assured Chen that the town had only ever had six berths. Yet the ticket named a seventh [[wharf|wharf]]. Chen pointed toward the bend: it had been the workers' name for a floating platform, not a registered permanent berth. Its absence from a new map did not mean it had never existed.","Under the desk lamp, another pencil line appeared on the ticket: 'When this job is finished, I'll take Azhou to see the sea.' I recognized Dad's [[handwriting|handwriting]], with its upward final stroke, but could not touch the paper. Cheng photographed both sides. Familiar writing alone could not [[identify|identify]] the sender, she reminded me. The ticket might be an [[authentic|authentic]] old object, while the new note came from someone alive today. We had to treat them separately. Zhao did not answer his phone. Chen had also waited in vain for him that morning. That was our first checkable [[clue|clue]].","The shop telephone rang. Zhao's wife said he had seemed to [[disappear|disappear]] after visiting the port building two nights earlier. He had mentioned checking material in the old [[archive|archive]]. She had already reported him missing. Officer He asked us to keep the mailing details and avoid pursuing anyone ourselves. Finding Zhao had suddenly become [[urgent|urgent]]. As I wrote down He's number, six bell strokes crossed the river. Half a minute later, a seventh sounded low in the rain, like a [[signal|signal]] from warehouse B. Chen caught my sleeve. 'That isn't the temple bell. Stay where there's light and listen first.'"]});
